@startuml possession-flow-shot
' ⚠ A DETAIL DIAGRAM. The whole possession, and the second-chance LOOP that
' wraps this one, are in possession-flow.puml — read that first.
' ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS: the three-way MAKE/MISS/BLOCK draw, the block recovery,
' the assist, and the and-1.
' ⚠ Notes say what the flow DOES; the argument lives in possession-flow-model.md.
' Render: plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng   (every diagram is now under
'   the 4096px default, so the flag is insurance — but keep using it, and ⚠ keep each
'   diagram SCREEN-SIZED: past ~2,000px it stops being readable long before it stops
'   rendering. ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out and does not catch deprecated syntax
'   that renders as a warning box — look at the PNG.)
title ShotResolver — make, miss, or block\n//§3.7 blocks · §3.11 and-1 · §3.21 block credits · §3.22 the putback assist//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start
:record FGA (+ 3PA if THREE);

switch (**one three-way draw**\n//offense skill for shot type vs defense//\n//P(BLOCK) carved off the top, own sensitivity//)
case (BLOCKED)
  :SHOT — BLOCKED_//shotType//
  missed FGA on the shooter
  **opponentPlayerId = the BLOCKER**, //recordBlock()//
  no assist;
  note right
     **Block = a field-goal outcome, exactly as a steal is a turnover outcome.** One three-way draw — no double-count.
    There is no PlayType.BLOCK.
    ⚠ **The blocker rides opponentPlayerId** (no new draw —
    `defender` was already selected).
    Reconciliation: count(BLOCKED% with opponent = X) == blocks(X).
  end note
  :**flat four-way loose-ball recovery**
  //fixed weights, defense-leaning — NOT the board contest//
  offense/defense × in-bounds/OOB;
  note right
    A blocked ball is a **chaotic loose ball**, not the
    box-out contest.
    ⚠ **THE FLAT ROLL PICKS A SIDE, NEVER A PLAYER.** Two
    different questions: *which side* is this flat roll; *which
    of that side's five* is a separate skill-weighted pick.
    ⚠ **The board contest is NEVER run here** — the side is
    already decided.
    ⚠ **COUNT THE EVENTS: a block emits TWO** — ``SHOT`` then
    ``REBOUND``, one of each, on every one of the four cases.
    Four MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE cases, not four events.
  end note
  if (recovered IN BOUNDS by the OFFENSE?) then (yes)
    :REBOUND — OFFENSIVE (credited)
    → **OFFENSE RETAINS** → second chance
    //this player becomes the putback candidate//;
    stop
  else (no)
    :REBOUND — DEFENSIVE, or OUT_OF_BOUNDS_*
    → **possession over**;
    stop
  endif

case (MADE)
  :SHOT — MADE_//shotType//
  +2 or +3 points;
  if (assisted?\n//teamOffense / passing of the four teammates//) then (yes)
    :assistPlayerId = the passer
    //recordAssist()//;
    note right
      ⚠ **A PUTBACK is assisted at HALF the ordinary chance, not zero**
      — nobody passed the rebounder his own board, but
      zeroing it would miss the assists row. The rule keys off
      `shooter == rebounder`, **NOT** "any second-chance shot":
      a kick-out three off an offensive rebound is an ordinary
      assisted basket.
    end note
  endif
  if (**and-1?**\n//shooter foulDrawing vs defender discipline//\n//× foulMultiplier(shotType) — the SAME shared table//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — AND_ONE  (+ the defender charged)
    :FREE_THROW ×**1** — *_AND_ONE
    //ONE for every shot type, a made three included//;
    note right
      ⚠ **The two foul rolls are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE** — the
      pre-shot FoulResolver branch **stops**, so a stopped shot
      never reaches here. One shot emits at most ONE of
      SHOOTING_FOUL / AND_ONE, never both.
      Where they DO compound is the period foul tally: both emit
      a FOUL and both count toward the bonus.
      An and-1 on a THREE is rarer **automatically** — the rolls
      are independent and the shot must ALSO go in.
      ⚠ **A missed live last FT here can RETAIN** — see
      possession-flow-foul.puml's live-board fork.
    end note
  endif
  :**possession over**;
  stop

case (MISSED)
  :→ on to the rebounding foul, then the board
  //possession-flow-rebound.puml//;
  stop
endswitch
@enduml
